135 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (The launch and deployment of AgriScanAI in Kakamega County was not just a product milestone. It was a field validation of how AI-driven systems can reshape agricultural decision-making. Working with the Kilimo Training Institute of Permaculture \(KTIP\), we onboarded over 100 smallholder farmers into a system designed to move agriculture from a reactive, fragmented and informal practice, into one that is predictive, data -driven, structured and measurable. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
136 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (For many, this was their first experience with AI in agriculture. But what followed was even more important. Farmers engaged with AgriScanAI capabilities such as AI-powered crop disease detection, Farm financial tracking and record-keeping, Localized advisory MwaneduAI and tracking of carbon emission and sequestration activities. But the most important shift was not technological. It was cognitive. Farmers began to ask deeper, system-oriented questions.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
137 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 523 0 R
/E (How do I optimize soil health over time?)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
